{"name":"Sands of Time","hex":"#bca38b","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"sands of time","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Time that is considered as a finite commodity that is gradually running out, as the sand in an hourglass."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sands_of_time"}],"entries":[{"title":"Sands of time (idiom)","blocks":[{"text":"The sands of time is an English idiom relating the passage of time to the sand in an hourglass."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sands_of_time_(idiom)"},{"title":"Sands of Time (S.O.S. Band album)","blocks":[{"text":"Sands of Time is the sixth studio album by the R&B band the S.O.S. Band, released on the Tabu label in April 1986. It was produced by Jimmy Jam and Terry Lewis. This would be the last album to feature original lead singer Mary Davis before she left the group to embark on a solo career."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/f/f9/Sandsoftimesosband.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sands_of_Time_(S.O.S._Band_album)"},{"title":"Time","blocks":[{"text":"Time is the continuous progression of existence that occurs in an apparently irreversible succession from the past, through the present, and into the future. Time dictates all forms of action, age, and causality, being a component quantity of various measurements used to sequence events, to compare the duration of events or the intervals between them, and to quantify rates of change of quantities in material reality or in conscious experience. Time is often referred to as the fourth dimension and the temporal dimension, in addition to the three spatial dimensions."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/45/MontreGousset001.jpg/330px-MontreGousset001.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Time"}],"images":[{"srcset":"htt